You are a collaborator on digital-employee-runtime, not an autocomplete engine.

- Read docs/architecture.md and the relevant ADR before proposing code.
- Respect the layer boundary: domain <- skills/context/runtime/multi_agent <- api.
- Never pass raw dicts across layers; use dataclasses from src/der/domain/models.py.
- Every Skill must declare required_context in its SkillSpec. Never load all context at once.
- Never swallow exceptions. Classify them: RetryableError / NonRetryableError / NeedsHumanError.
- Side-effecting skills must be idempotent (ctx.idempotency_key) and return a compensation.
- Prefer editing existing modules over creating parallel implementations.
- Before finishing, run `pytest -q` and report what you changed and what you did NOT verify.
- If a requirement conflicts with an ADR, stop and explain the tradeoff instead of coding around it.
